  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev05-04",
    "question": "<p>(i) Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in\\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\\\ -1 &amp; 5 \\end{array} \\right)^{n}=\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\left( 5^{n}-1 \\right) &amp; 5^{n} \\end{array} \\right)\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p><p>(ii) Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in\\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\left( 2r-1 \\right)^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}n\\left( 4n^{2}-1 \\right)\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>In the matrix argument take the lower-left dot product using the first column <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-1)\"></span>. In the separate sum argument the next odd number after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k-1\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+1\"></span>. This is why the induction step adds <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k+1)^2\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(i) At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-(5-1)/4=-1\"></span>, so the stated matrix equals <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume the expression holds when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^{k+1}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\-(5^k-1)/4&amp;5^k\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;0\\\\-1&amp;5\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The first row is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\"></span> and the bottom-right entry is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^{k+1}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The bottom-left entry is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-(5^k-1)/4-5^k=-(5^{k+1}-1)/4\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>This proves the induction step and hence the formula for every positive integer. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\"></span> both sides are 1. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_k=k(4k^2-1)/3\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Add the next term <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k+1)^2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Factor to give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k+1)[k(2k-1)+3(2k+1)]/3\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Inside the brackets, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k^2+5k+3=(k+1)(2k+3)\"></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_{k+1}=(k+1)[4(k+1)^2-1]/3\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The base case and inductive implication establish the result for every positive integer. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 12 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev05-04-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2015 · Q6, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev05-05",
    "question": "<p>Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(n)=8^{n}-2^{n}\"></span> is divisible by 6 <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The useful multiplier is visible from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8^{k+1}=8\\cdot8^k\"></span>. Subtracting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8f(k)\"></span> cancels that whole power. The terms in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^k\"></span> then have coefficient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8-2=6\"></span>, yielding a multiple of the desired divisor.</p>",
      "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=8-2=6\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8^k-2^k=6m\"></span> for some integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=8\\cdot8^k-2\\cdot2^k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Subtract <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8f(k)\"></span> to leave <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\cdot2^k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=6(8m+2^k)\"></span> is divisible by 6. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The result follows for every positive integer by induction. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev05-05-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2014 · Q9, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev05-06",
    "question": "<p>(a) Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} (r+1)2^{r-1}=n2^{n}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The sum through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k+1\"></span> contains the entire sum through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> plus the single term at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=k+1\"></span>. In that new term <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r+1=k+2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r-1=k\"></span>. Both contributions now contain <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^k\"></span>, leaving the simple coefficient <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k+(k+2)\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\"></span> the sum and the proposed expression both equal 2. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_k=\\sum_{r=1}^k(r+1)2^{r-1}=k2^k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>On adding the next term, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_{k+1}=k2^k+(k+2)2^k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Collecting powers gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k+2)2^k=(k+1)2^{k+1}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence the formula propagates from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k+1\"></span> and holds by induction for every positive integer. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 5 marks.</p>",
      "<p>Count only the retained parts. Any original whole-question total on the extract belongs to the complete exam question.</p>",
