  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev05-07",
    "question": "<p>(a) A sequence of numbers is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"u_{1}=8\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"u_{n+1}=4 u_{n}-9 n, \\quad n \\geqslant 1\"></div><p>Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"u_{n}=4^{n}+3 n+1\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(b) Prove by induction that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} 3 &amp; -4 \\\\ 1 &amp; -1 \\end{array} \\right)^{m}=\\left( \\begin{array}{cc} 2 m+1 &amp; -4 m \\\\ m &amp; 1-2 m \\end{array} \\right)\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>In the recurrence the linear term <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12k-9k\"></span> leaves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3k\"></span>, and the remaining constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\"></span> supplies the required shift to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(k+1)+1\"></span>. In the matrix argument compare entries with the claimed matrix after replacing every <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k+1\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4+3+1=8=u_1\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_k=4^k+3k+1\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u_{k+1}=4(4^k+3k+1)-9k=4^{k+1}+3k+4\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>This equals <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4^{k+1}+3(k+1)+1\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence the formula follows by induction. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=1\"></span> the right side equals the given matrix. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Assume the formula for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Multiply <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^k\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> to give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}3(2k+1)-4k&amp;-4(2k+1)+4k\\\\3k+1-2k&amp;-4k-1+2k\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>This is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}2(k+1)+1&amp;-4(k+1)\\\\k+1&amp;1-2(k+1)\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>By induction the identity holds for every positive integer. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
